<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 28 August, from 475 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">475 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,551 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orestes drives Western Emperor Julius Nepos from Ravenna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> seized Ravenna and Julius Nepos fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>. Orestes then made his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a> emperor; he would be the last to rule in the West.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1565">1565 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">461 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pedro Menéndez sights Florida and names it for St Augustine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-menendez-de-aviles">Pedro Menéndez de Avilés</a> sighted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> coast on the feast of St Augustine and gave the saint's name to the harbour. He founded the settlement on 8 September; it is the oldest continuously occupied European city in the US.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First issue of Scientific American is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Inventor Rufus Porter launched Scientific American as a weekly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. It is the oldest continuously published monthly magazine in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther King gives his 'I Have a Dream' speech</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking to some 250,000 people at the March on Washington, King described his dream of a nation free from racial injustice. The march helped build support for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civil-rights-act-of-1964">Civil Rights Act of 1964</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2005">2005 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">21 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Orleans orders its first mandatory evacuation as Katrina nears</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With Hurricane Katrina at Category 5 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>, Mayor Ray Nagin ordered the city's first-ever mandatory evacuation. Tens of thousands without transport sheltered in the Superdome.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li></ol>
